# The tool versions of the Linux CI image, and of the continuous build that
# installs the same tools without the image. This file is the one place they
# are stated.
#
# The image takes every build tool from the Ubuntu image itself: no third-party
# repository and no downloaded archive. A tool the image ships is a tool a
# developer on the same release can install, so a warning the CI reports is a
# warning anyone can reproduce. A version is only overridden here when the
# image ships one too old to build the project. PostgreSQL is the one package
# that comes from elsewhere, because the archive build of it fails this
# project's queries; the Dockerfile states which versions and why.
#
# To move to a new compiler or tool:
#   1. Change its line below.
#   2. Run build/docker/ci/build.sh. It builds the image and prints its tag.
#   3. Commit this file with the change.
#
# LLVM_MAJOR and GCC_MAJOR name the versioned packages the image installs.
# GCC_MAJOR is also the C++ standard library clang links against: clang uses
# the newest GCC it finds.
UBUNTU_VERSION=26.04
LLVM_MAJOR=21
GCC_MAJOR=16
PG_MAJOR=18
